  "body": "Found by the QA runs of 2026-11-18 (SolidCraft v0.44.1 designs -> CamCraft main `83867fd7`), parts p06 (all-ops mill part) and p07 (lathe shaft); both have fillets or blend faces.\n\nWhat happens: `import_model <design>.sc` refuses the design:\n`Solidcraft design refused: import_solidcraft: invalid input: the final body does not decode: native B-rep: unknown variant 'blend', expected one of 'plane', ..., 'placed_revolution'`.\n\nSolidCraft 0.44 writes a `blend` surface kind that CamCraft's `.sc` reader (#1456) does not know. Designs without fillets import. Every design with a fillet, round or blend - most real parts - is refused, so the \"open SolidCraft files directly\" path does not work for them.\n\nWorkarounds today: export STEP from SolidCraft (but see the STEP mesh-gap issue the same runs found) or STL.\n\nDone means: a `.sc` design with fillets from the current SolidCraft release imports with the same body as its STEP export (a pinned fixture `.sc` with a blend face, and a test). Track the next SolidCraft surface kinds the same way (the QA runs re-check each SolidCraft release).\n",
